      "citations": null,
      "text": "The gate acts on 4 qubits (`2 ** 4`), and the two slices supply 1 + 3 = 4 qubits. The bug is in how they are passed. `circ.append(gate, qr1[1:2], qr2[0:3])` treats the second slice as `cargs`, which expects classical bits, so the call fails. Concatenating both slices into a single qubit list fixes it.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumRegister, QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit.extensions import UnitaryGate\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import random_unitary\n\ngate = UnitaryGate(random_unitary(2 ** 4).data, 'RND-U16')\n\nqr1 = QuantumRegister(2, 'q')\nqr2 = QuantumRegister(3, 'a')\n\ncirc = QuantumCircuit(qr1, qr2)\n\n# FIX: second register slice was passed as cargs (classical bits) -> concatenated both qubit slices into one qargs list, because the gate needs all 4 qubits as quantum arguments\ncirc.append(gate, qr1[1:2] + qr2[0:3])\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
